ternal expectations. Art and music should ultimately be about how they resonate with you and the experiences you wish to share with others. It’s fascinating how different forms of expression can sometimes become shackled by the very audience they aim to reach, leading to a disconnect that stifles creativity. What about music theory? Have you revisited that? Diving into the intricacies of music theory can be a great way to reconnect with your love for music without the external pressures, allowing you to explore harmonies, rhythms, and even the cultural context that often informs those Pacific Island texts and rhythms. It can serve as a method of grounding your creativity, giving you new tools to articulate your feelings and thoughts about music in a more enriching way."
